Subject: [PATCH] build: declare trust roots for authenticated Cargo acquisition
Origin: other, Peios catalogue qualification review
Upstream-Status: Pending [declare the TLS trust-store dependency of cargo vendor]

The minimal Debian root installs no recommended packages. Cargo uses libgit2
to fetch locked HTTPS Git sources, which requires a CA trust store. Declare
ca-certificates explicitly; retain certificate validation and locked source
identities. No git CLI dependency is needed for this libgit2 acquisition path.

--- a/pekit.toml
+++ b/pekit.toml
@@ -52,6 +52,7 @@
 "org.python.python3"              = "*"
 
 [build.vendor.dependencies.apt]
+ca-certificates = "*"
 cargo     = "*"
 rustc     = "*"
 python3   = "*"
